## 1. Overview & Background

### What is the Agentic AI Foundation Platform?

The **Agentic AI Foundation Platform** — referred to as the **AI Landing Zone (AI LZ)** — is a standardised, secure, and scalable platform blueprint enabling teams to build and deliver Generative AI (GenAI) and Agentic AI solutions consistently across the enterprise.

It extends existing investments in strategic AI/ML, strategic GenAI (AIaaS), and cloud platform foundations. It leverages enterprise-wide shared services:

- **AKS** — compute for agent runtimes
- **Redis** — short-term conversational memory
- **Kafka** — event-driven agent patterns
- **APIM** — API gateway for all agent traffic
- **Ada / OTel** — observability and telemetry

It further integrates with:

- **Entra ID** — agent and workload identity
- **Azure Policy / Defender** — cloud security posture
- **SIEM** — security event monitoring
- **JFrog/Artifactory** — SDK distribution
- **Azure DevOps** — CI/CD pipelines

### Why Build This?

The platform addresses observed challenges in the AI delivery landscape:

- Fragmented implementation patterns across teams
- Extended proof-of-concept cycles
- Inconsistent security and compliance controls
- Re-implementation of foundational concerns per use case

By converging onto a unified design, the organisation can:

- Reduce solution complexity
- Improve time-to-value
- Strengthen compliance alignment
- Enable safe integration of agents into the broader data and application ecosystem

### High-Level Platform Capabilities

**Delivered:**

- Standardised platform blueprint for agentic workloads (AI Landing Zone)
- Operational and cybersecurity observability by design, end-to-end
- Identity-centric security with least privilege
- Standardised agent lifecycle management
- Secure, consistent runtime memory
- Clear boundary between memory and workflow state
- Governed tool ecosystem for agents (MCP Server pattern)
- Release-grade human evaluation
- Capability hosts and governance (Vector Database)

**Future Extension (not yet elaborated):**

- Workflow Orchestration (Agentic BPM)
- Agent Business Performance (KPI Measurement)
- AI Agent DevSecOps
- Machine Identity Visibility (SailPoint)
- AI Firewall integration

