## 5. Security & Governance

### Five Security Lenses

The security posture is described across five standard lenses plus a sixth for SDK-specific supply chain concerns:

#### 5.1 Network

- SDK is an outbound client only — no inbound listener or network service
- All A2A traffic routes through APIM (no direct agent-to-external-agent communication)
- Outbound egress constrained to an allow-list of registered FQDNs
- New egress routes assessed individually per external agent onboarding
- No SSE streaming through APIM (APIM buffers responses — streaming requires exception approval)

#### 5.2 Identity

- `get_credential()` resolution hierarchy enforced at SDK level
- Deployed workloads use Managed Identity; fail-fast if not running under approved identity
- CI/CD operations use separate pipeline identity (`kind="cli"` with OIDC)
- Agent Blueprints and Agent Identities automatically created in Entra when agents are created in Foundry
- SDK holds no secrets in code

#### 5.3 Data

- `ColesAgentConfig` provides field-stable interface across secret injection mechanism changes
- Fail-fast validation surfaces misconfiguration before service connections
- Short-term memory follows key-naming conventions (`agent_id:orchestration_id:thread_id`)
- `enable_sensitive_data` flag (defaults `True`) controls whether prompts/responses are captured in OTel spans — review against data classification before enabling
- PII/payload redaction is a use-case application responsibility

#### 5.4 AI-Specific Security

- A2A responses treated as **untrusted external content** — screened via Azure AI Content Safety (Prompt Shields) before re-entering agent reasoning
- Outbound messages screened for adversarial content before forwarding to external agents
- Grounding and authority boundary: A2A responses are input for reasoning, not privileged instructions
- Agent card integrity validated at onboarding; weekly change-detection pipeline monitors registered agents
- SDK does not expose any mechanism to override, bypass, or weaken mandatory backend security baseline

**Key threat:** Prompt injection via A2A responses from a compromised external agent embedding instructions designed to hijack Coles agent behaviour.

#### 5.5 Monitoring

- All security-relevant events forwarded to SIEM
- SDK emits structured stdout JSON logs + OTel traces consumed by AKS sidecar
- `ErrorLoggingMiddleware` always active on all agents; stamps `orchestration_id` on every event
- A2A-specific log fields: `a2a.task_id`, `a2a.context_id`, `a2a.task_state`, transport errors

**Correlation fields across A2A traffic:**

| Field | Source |
|---|---|
| `gen_ai.operation.name` | `invoke_agent` (constant) |
| `gen_ai.provider.name` | `A2A` (constant) |
| `gen_ai.agent.name` | Registered external agent name |
| `server.address` | APIM-fronted URL |
| `orchestration_id` | Coles workflow correlation ID |
| `a2a.task_id` | A2A continuation token / task ID |
| `a2a.context_id` | A2A context ID |
| `a2a.task_state` | `completed` / `failed` / `canceled` / `rejected` |

#### 5.6 Software Supply Chain and SDK Integrity

- SDK distributed exclusively via approved JFrog/Artifactory feed
- Scaffolded `pyproject.toml` pins JFrog as the only allowed package source — prevents dependency confusion from public PyPI
- MAF and third-party dependencies pinned to approved version ranges
- Capability modules resolvable only from approved feed; must be published and catalogued by Data & AI team
- All modules undergo SCA, IaC, SAST, and secrets scans before publishing

### APIM Security Controls

| Control | Scope | Detail |
|---|---|---|
| Token validation | Inherited (global/product) | `validate-azure-ad-token` — verifies issuer, audience, expiry, tenant, calling-application identity |
| App Role authorisation | Per integration (API scope) | Per-agent app role validates caller entitlement |
| Base rate limiting | Inherited (product) | Applies to all APIs in product |
| Agent-identity rate limiting | Per integration | `rate-limit-by-key` on calling agent managed identity |
| Retry | Per integration | Exponential backoff on transient 429/5xx — app code does not implement retry loops |
| Circuit breaker | Per integration (backend) | Trips on sustained failures; returns 503 (APIM v2 tier required) |
| Timeout | Per integration | Defaults to 30s per integration (not APIM default 300s) |

### API Center Registration

Every external A2A agent registered in Azure API Center with mandatory metadata:

- Type, Protocol, Boundary (External), Direction (Outbound)
- Name, Vendor, Owner, Purpose, Version
- APIM proxy URL, Data Owner
- Permitted data classifications, Approved data exchange profile
- Data classification, Data residency
- Monitoring coverage, Agent card URL, Status (Active/Retired)

