## 9. Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **AI Landing Zone (AI LZ)** | The standardised, secure, scalable infrastructure blueprint for agentic AI workloads, layered on the Enterprise Landing Zone |
| **A2A (Agent-to-Agent)** | Open protocol for communication between agents across process, service, and organisational boundaries via HTTP |
| **Agent Card** | Metadata document published by an external agent describing its capabilities, skills, supported input/output modes, security schemes, and endpoint URL |
| **APIM** | Azure API Management — the central gateway for all API traffic (REST, MCP, A2A, GraphQL) |
| **Coles Agentic SDK** | The Python package and CLI providing standardised, governed foundational concerns for building MAF/Foundry-based agents |
| **Foundry Agent Service** | Azure AI Foundry's managed agent runtime — hosts Prompt Agent definitions and orchestrates model calls |
| **MAF (Microsoft Agent Framework)** | Microsoft-provided Python framework (`agent-framework-core`, `agent-framework-foundry`) |
| **MCP (Model Context Protocol)** | Protocol enabling agents to safely invoke tools against internal platforms and business systems via a governed server endpoint |
| **Orchestration ID** | Workflow-level correlation identifier stamped on all structured events to enable cross-component log correlation |
| **Path 1** | Foundry Agent Service A2A tool integration — model-driven, Public Preview, not recommended for production |
| **Path 2** | MAF code-level A2A integration — orchestrator-driven, GA, recommended default |
| **Prompt Agent** | An agent definition (instructions, model, tools) created and versioned in Azure AI Foundry |
| **Short-term Memory** | Per-agent, per-thread conversational state stored in Azure Managed Redis with TTL; key-prefix isolation enforced at orchestrator |
| **Trust Boundary** | The perimeter within which systems are assumed to be governed and monitored. External A2A agents always remain outside this boundary regardless of TLS/auth controls |
